Subject: [PATCH 2/3] =?UTF-8?q?=F0=9F=90=9B=20Fix=20charging=20indicator?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20and=20add=20Battery=20settings=20on=20Android?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The status bar showed the charging bolt from battery_plus, which asks
the battery HAL for BATTERY_PROPERTY_STATUS and ignores whether a
charger is attached. It also only re-read the level when that status
changed.

Read the sticky ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED broadcast instead, through a
small local plugin (packages/classipod_power), the same source the
system status bar uses:
- nothing plugged in is never charging, whatever the status says;
- plugged in but the level falling, or not rising for 15 minutes,
  counts as not charging (Battery Care hold, or a USB port weaker
  than the screen's draw);
- with Sony's Battery Care on, 90% and above counts as not charging;
- the level updates on every broadcast.

Add Settings > Battery (Android only) so power settings that were
being changed over adb live in the app:
- Status, opening the system battery usage page;
- Battery Saver (global low_power);
- Battery Care: the settings tables are scanned for Sony's switch,
  which isn't documented; if it can't be found or written, the item
  opens the system Battery page;
- Bluetooth Scanning (global ble_scan_always_enabled);
- Screen Timeout (system screen_off_timeout).

Android only lets third-party apps write these after a one-time
`adb shell pm grant <package> android.permission.WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS`;
until then the screen shows an Allow Changes item explaining it.

